<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA PLACES 5 T-BILL ISSUES WORTH 24.7 BLN LVS.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA PLACES 5 T-BILL ISSUES WORTH 24.7 BLN LVS.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry placed</p>
<p>five special T-bill issues with maturity between 15 and 85</p>
<p>days, worth a total of 24.705 billion levs, the central bank</p>
<p>said.</p>
<p>Four of the issues were discount ones, the fifth had a</p>
<p>floater coupon equal to the central bank's main interest rate</p>
<p>(CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 16.50</p>
<p>percent monthly or 198 percent annually.</p>
<p>In line with its usual practice the central bank did not</p>
<p>say with which financial intitution or institutions the issues</p>
<p>were placed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Prices are in percent of par.</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3017297022	 BG3017397004</p>
<p> Type			    floater coupon     discount</p>
<p> Term			    85 days		15 days</p>
<p> Issue date		    February 19, 1997  February 19, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 May 15, 1997	 March 6, 1997</p>
<p> Par value		     2,820 mln levs     5,400 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg sales price	     88.75 pct	    92.35 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     64.63 pct	    8.28 pct</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3017497002	 BG3017597009</p>
<p> Type			    discount	     discount</p>
<p> Term			    16 days		19 days</p>
<p> Issue date		    February 19, 1997  February 19, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 March 7, 1997	March 10, 1997</p>
<p> Par value		     5,400 mln levs     5,530 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg sales price	     91.90 pct	    90.40 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     8.81 pct	     10.62 pct</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3017697007</p>
<p> Type			    discount</p>
<p> Term			    20 days</p>
<p> Issue date		    February 19, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 March 11, 1997</p>
<p> Par value		     5,555 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg sales price	     90.00 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     11.11 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
